Footprinting with WHOIS, DNS & Web Tools
I performed reconnaissance on networkwalks.com using six Kali Linux tools:
WHOIS → Registrar, name servers, domain dates
WhatWeb → WordPress 7.0.4, WP Download Manager 3.3.58
nslookup → IP resolved to 192.232.216.135
curl -I → HTTP headers, caching, cookies, /wp-json/ endpoint
wafw00f → Detected ModSecurity (SpiderLabs)
dnsrecon → NS, MX, SPF/TXT, SRV records
Why this matters:  
Footprinting reveals the attack surface, technologies, DNS structure, and potential misconfigurations.
